# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings, whatever the checkout platform.
#
# scripts/deploy/build-linux.sh runs inside a Linux container from a Windows bind mount. With CRLF
# endings the container fails on `\r: command not found` — an error that reads like a missing
# binary rather than a line-ending problem, and which cost a manual `sed -i 's/\r$//'` on every
# copy of the build script during the 2026-09-01 recovery.
#
# core.autocrlf on a Windows clone would otherwise rewrite these on checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else executed by a Linux runtime.
*.bash text eol=lf
